//? Title: Triplet learning with strict semi-hard negatives
//? Subtitle: Tensor computations, explicit checks and reproducible local figures
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Unit embeddings make similarity a squared-distance problem. Independent normalization,maxout and triplet derivatives precede full NN1 execution,actual class-balanced MNIST previews and visible detached mining plus tensor Adam fitting. Restored class-disjoint evaluation includes calibrated verification and actual retrieval episodes.
)
\toc

Source example: `examples/cpp/source/nn/1_convolutional_neural_networks/1.8_other_vision_tasks/facenet_triplet.cpp`.

> The method

Learn128D unit embeddings by pulling an anchor toward a same-class positive while requiring a different-class negative to lie beyond a margin. Mine only strict semi-hard negatives from frozen current embeddings,recompute their gradient graph,and choose a checkpoint on unseen validation classes.

The editable concept diagram is `diagrams/facenet_triplet_concept.tikz`. Regeneration uses
LaTeX with PGF/TikZ and standalone, plus dvisvgm; exports use the saved SVG.

```{bash, results="output", file="figures/facenet_triplet_concept.svg"}
set -eu
mkdir -p build
latex -interaction=batchmode -halt-on-error -output-directory=build diagrams/facenet_triplet_concept.tikz > build/facenet_triplet_concept.compile.log 2>&1
dvisvgm --no-fonts --bbox=10 --output=build/facenet_triplet_concept.svg build/facenet_triplet_concept.dvi > build/facenet_triplet_concept.render.log 2>&1
printf 'Rendered local concept diagram.\n'
```
