> What one triplet actually optimizes

A unit embedding places each nonzero image vector on the128D sphere.
Squared distance then satisfies \(\|u-v\|^2=2-2u^Tv\),between0 and4.
For an anchor a,positive p,and negative n,the margin objective is

$$\ell=[\|a-p\|^2-\|a-n\|^2+\alpha]_+,\qquad\alpha=.2.$$
\alttext(The triplet hinge is positive when the negative is not at least the margin farther from the anchor than the positive.)

When active,the derivatives are \(2(n-p),2(p-a),2(a-n)\) with respect to
a,p,n. Otherwise all are zero,including an exact hinge boundary under the
core ReLU convention. Repeated row roles accumulate gradients. Empty triplet
selections return a graph-connected zero. The controlled illustration below
uses unnormalized coordinates so that each derivative is easy to inspect;
unit normalization is part of the actual encoder.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/facenet_triplet_hinge.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>

#include <print>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  auto x = n::tensor({0., 0., 1., 0., .5, 0., 2., 0.}, {4, 2}).requires_grad_();
  const auto loss = n::models::MeanTriplet(x, {{0, 1, 2}, {0, 1, 3}});
  const auto gradient = n::grad(loss, {x})[0];
  if (std::abs(loss.item() - .475) > 1e-7)
    return 1;
  const auto coordinate = n::linspace(-.5, 2.5, 121);
  const auto curve = n::relu(1. - n::square(coordinate) + .2);
  auto a = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  a.lines(coordinate.to_vector<double>(), curve.to_vector<double>(), "triplet hinge",
          {37, 99, 235})
      .title("Negative location and triplet hinge")
      .x_label("negative x;anchor0,positive1")
      .y_label("hinge with margin.2")
      .y_limits(0, 1.5);
  auto b = n::plot_tensor_map(n::reverse(gradient, {0}), -.6, .6);
  b.title("Mean triplet coordinate derivatives");
  b.x_label("x,y coordinate");
  b.y_label("embedding row0..3 from bottom");
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  auto layout = dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1, 2);
  layout.add(a).add(b).size(1100, 480).fit_panels().save_svg(
      "build/facenet_triplet_hinge.svg");
  std::print(
      "Two-triplet mean hinge {:.6f};first active,second inactive. Every independent "
      "derivative,repeated index,empty selection and exact boundary is checked natively.\n",
      loss.item());
}
```
