> NN1 normalization,maxout and full-width execution

The NN1-style encoder retains eleven SAME ReLU convolutions,two LRN stages,
four3x3/stride2 SAME pools,two adjacent-pair maxout dense layers,a linear128D
head,and squared-norm-floored unit normalization. LRN uses radius2,bias1,
alpha1e-4,beta.75. Equal maxout inputs split their gradient equally. A zero
embedding stays zero;below the squared-norm floor epsilon1e-12,the derivative
is identity/sqrt(epsilon). The native independent oracle covers zero/floored
normalization,unique/tied maxout and every triplet-coordinate derivative.

The full220pxRGB graph has140,025,664 learned scalars/28 leaves. Unlike a
shape-only census,the following block allocates it and executes one complete
forward/backward pass. The compact28px grayscale model divides every conv
width by8 and uses128-unit maxouts,retaining all13 recorded stages and128D
output:108,040 learned scalars/28 leaves. Initializers,compact widths,LRN
constants,padding and Adam are teaching choices;there are no pretrained face
weights,BN moving moments or claimed face-recognition benchmarks.

```{cpp, results="markdown", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>

#include <print>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  namespace m = n::models;
  n::set_num_threads(2);
  for (bool compact : {false, true}) {
    const auto c = compact ? m::FaceNetConfig::Compact() : m::FaceNetConfig{};
    n::ParameterStore p(17);
    const int batch = compact ? 2 : 1;
    const auto input = .5 + .45 * n::sin(n::arange(0, batch * c.side * c.side * c.input)
                                             .reshape({batch, c.side, c.side, c.input}) *
                                         .113);
    const auto out = m::FaceNetNN1(p, input, c);
    const auto weights = n::sin(n::arange(0, batch * 128).reshape({batch, 128}) * .17);
    const auto gradients = n::grad(n::sum(out.embedding * weights), p.parameters());
    if (p.count() != (compact ? 108040 : 140025664) || p.count() != m::FaceNetCensus(c) ||
        gradients.size() != 28)
      return 1;
    double smallest = INFINITY;
    for (const auto &g : gradients) {
      if (!g.defined())
        return 1;
      const double norm = n::norm(g).item();
      if (!std::isfinite(norm))
        return 1;
      smallest = std::min(smallest, norm);
    }
    if (compact && smallest <= 0)
      return 1;
    const auto norms = n::sum(n::square(out.embedding.to(n::DType::Float64)), {1});
    if (n::max(n::abs(norms - 1.)).item() > 2e-6)
      return 1;
    std::print("{} NN1:{} learned scalars,28 finite gradients,13 stages,128D unit "
               "output;smallest gradient norm {:.6g}. No fitting in this check.\n",
               compact ? "Compact28" : "Full220RGB", p.count(), smallest);
  }
}
```
